---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Nuclear Physics Cheat Sheet | Free Radioactivity, Fission, Fusion"
  description="Complete nuclear physics cheat sheet with radioactivity, fission, and fusion. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Nuclear Physics<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Radioactivity, fission, and fusion. From atomic structure to nuclear energy.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Radioactivity</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Decay Laws</h3>
        <pre><code>N = N₀e^(-λt)
A = λN (activity)
t₁/₂ = ln(2)/λ (half-life)
λ = ln(2)/t₁/₂</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Types of Radiation</h3>
        <pre><code>α: ⁴₂He (2p + 2n)
β⁻: e⁻ (neutron → proton)
β⁺: e⁺ (proton → neutron)
γ: electromagnetic (no mass/charge)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mass-Energy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Einstein's Equation</h3>
        <pre><code>E = mc²
ΔE = Δmc²
1 u = 931.5 MeV/c²
Mass defect: Δm = Σm_products - Σm_reactants</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Nuclear Fission</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fission Process</h3>
        <pre><code>²³⁵U + n → ²³⁶U* → fission products + 2-3n + energy
Chain reaction: neutrons cause more fissions
Critical mass: minimum for sustained reaction
Energy per fission: ~200 MeV</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Nuclear Fusion</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fusion Process</h3>
        <pre><code>²H + ³H → ⁴He + n + 17.6 MeV
Requires: high T (>10⁷ K), high pressure
Energy per fusion: ~17.6 MeV
Sun: pp chain, CNO cycle</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
